@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 6
skinparam defaultFontName "Segoe UI"
skinparam defaultFontSize 12

title Weather Data Integration Connector

actor User

package "Entrypoints" {
  component "CLI\napp.cli" as CLI
  component "FastAPI\napp.api" as API
}

package "Validation and ETL" {
  component "Input and API Models\nCityInput, WeatherRunRequest" as InputModels
  component "Open-Meteo and Domain Models\nOpenMeteo*Response, WeatherRecord" as DataModels
  component "Pipeline\nrun_weather_pipeline" as Pipeline
  component "Concurrent Extractor\napp.extractor" as Extractor
  component "HTTPS Client\napp.client" as Client
  component "Pandas Transformer\napp.transformer" as Transformer
}

package "Outputs" {
  interface "DataSink" as DataSink
  component "Atomic CSV Exporter\napp.exporter" as CSVExporter
  component "Matplotlib Renderer\ngenerate_weather_chart\napp.visualizer" as ChartRenderer
  database "Configured Output Directory\nweather_data.csv\nweather_chart.png" as Output
}

cloud "Open-Meteo Services" {
  component "Geocoding API\n/v1/search" as Geocoding
  component "Forecast API\n/v1/forecast" as Forecast
}

User --> CLI : --cities, --sort-by,\n--output-dir
User --> API : HTTP requests
CLI --> InputModels : validate city names
API --> InputModels : validate bounded run request
CLI --> Pipeline : run ETL
API --> Pipeline : POST /integrations/weather/run

Pipeline --> Extractor : extract_batch
Extractor --> Client : private HTTPS session per worker
Client --> Geocoding : HTTPS, timeout, retries,\nredirects disabled
Client --> Forecast : HTTPS, Celsius and m/s
Geocoding --> Extractor : geocoding results
Forecast --> Extractor : current and current_units
Extractor --> DataModels : validate upstream payloads
Extractor --> Pipeline : WeatherRecord list
Pipeline --> Transformer : transform and rank
Transformer --> DataSink : canonical weather DataFrame
DataSink <|.. CSVExporter
CSVExporter --> Output : formula-safe atomic CSV

API --> Output : GET /integrations/weather/export\nread CSV for chart requests
Output --> API : weather_data.csv
API --> ChartRenderer : validated CSV and chart_type
ChartRenderer --> API : in-memory PNG bytes
ChartRenderer --> Output : optional PNG file output
API --> User : CSV or image/png response

note right of API
GET /health
POST /integrations/weather/run
GET /integrations/weather/export
GET /integrations/weather/chart
  ?chart_type=bar|scatter|dashboard|heatmap

The chart endpoint reads the existing CSV
and does not call Open-Meteo.
Optional API_KEY authentication protects
the run endpoint.
end note

note bottom of ChartRenderer
Matplotlib Agg backend
Bar, scatter, 1x3 dashboard, heatmap
Figures are closed after rendering.
end note

@enduml
